 Staged print sink. __serial_put takes the byte in AL and clobbers only
 RDX and flags, the same surface as the wait-and-out triple it replaces.
 When the boot probe found the codex-vm blit (flag cell 36176) the byte
 is staged at the cursor cell 36192 instead of leaving through the UART
 - no VM exit. Anywhere else the legacy LSR-poll-and-OUT runs. The
 __print_begin and __print_flush brackets anchor the staging region at
 the heap top (R10 scratch; nothing allocates during a print) and blit
 the whole print in one doorbell. Single-writer discipline: the BSP
 owns the cells; concurrent AP prints were already garbled per-byte and
 remain unsupported.

