Section: UEFI Console Helpers

  uefi-load-conout : List Integer

  uefi-load-conout = [72, 139, 4, 37] & write-i32 uefi-systab-addr & [72, 139, 72, 64]

 The Microsoft x64 convention firmware is called under requires 32 bytes of
 shadow space and RSP 16-byte aligned at the call. RBX is saved because it is
 callee-saved on OUR side and this sequence overwrites it with the protocol
 pointer; the shadow space is 32 rather than 40 because the second push already
 supplies the 8 bytes that kept the alignment before it existed.

  uefi-call-conout : Integer -> List Integer

  uefi-call-conout (func-offset) =

    [65, 82, 83, 72, 137, 203, 72, 131, 236, 32] & [255, 83, func-offset] & [72, 131, 196, 32, 91, 65, 90]

  emit-uefi-set-attr-helper : CodegenState -> CodegenState

