 peek-byte, poke-byte and peek-qword carry the same window guard as
 peek-32 / poke-32. Without it a byte-wise or qword writer would reach
 the rasterizer's command buffer at 0xBE000000 without earning
 cap-gpu-memory -- the guard is on the sanctioned write path, not the
 access width, so every width that can touch the window is gated. The
 guard is the same three-ALU-op top-byte test, and it costs peek-qword
 (a memo-table primitive) the same predicted, memory-free branch it
 costs peek-32.

